# SuperAgent project rules

`AGENTS.md` is the canonical complete rule set and must be read before changing
this repository. Keep `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, and these Cursor rules
semantically synchronized.

- SuperAgent is a production application on the released Dex Go SDK, not an SDK
  example. Do not depend on Dex internals or unreleased APIs.
- Do not add compatibility shims before launch.
- Use constructor injection, typed domain values, explicit boundary mappers,
  owned goroutines, and handled errors.
- Keep documentation direct. Put one idea in each sentence. Split behavior,
  constraints, and rationale into separate sentences.
- Do not introduce `NormalizeXyz` identifiers. Name the concrete operation.
- Test-only APIs must include `ForTestOnly` in their identifiers. Prefer test-only source files.
- Reuse existing repository and public API terms exactly in identifiers.
- Domain packages prohibit `any`, dynamic maps, and raw string states.
- Never export Dex resource getters solely to expose descriptors.
- Keep provider, MCP, Dex, application, transport, and UI boundaries separate.
- Assume a second consumer (SuperVerse Studio / agent-server). Application-
  visible conversation UI, merge/sort helpers, and Tool presentation belong in
  `@superdurable/superagent-ui` with `sa-*` / slots; portal `web/src` stays
  transport, orchestration, branding, and thin mappers. Do not ship portal-only
  UI to extract later. Public Go/OpenAPI surfaces stay in `agent` / `model`.
- Never commit or log `.env` or credentials.
- Every changing turn ends with a meaningful commit and clean worktree.
